md='# Provenance and copied-material license audit\n\nThe complete catalog reconciles **43 repositories, 20 owned, 74 source entries, 108 retained historical attribution records and 100 linked distinct attribution IDs**. Every mapped product file exists and every linked ID resolves. All 47 distinct declared repository/SHA source pairs independently resolve via precise public GitHub Git commit APIs. Every exact selected source path/pin was checked against its declared commit tree; all 47 trees were complete and no nonexistent selected path or selected blob mismatch was found. The additional nested RVR origin is independently resolved at`549a7e150ddc75df88dc90ee93f331fea7464567`, distinct from the generic adapter pin.\n\nAll 77 copied upstream files match local SHA256, Git blob and size declarations and original declared upstream tree membership. 19 nested-origin files separately match Crystal, RVR and Semantic ABI original pinned trees. Seven copied npm legal notices match the fresh candidate\'s own installed license bytes, versions and lock declarations. New productLICENSE SHA256 is`cfc7749b96f63bd31c3c42b5c471bf756814053e847c10f3eb003417bc523d30`; NOTICE names Copyright 2026 Pavlo Tvardovskyi and preserves upstream exclusions. No license issue was found in actually copied material. This assessment concerns copied material and new product bytes only; it does not reopen license cleanup for unselected repositories.\n\nRepository ownership does not establish code authorship. Review/finding/requirements attribution is kept separate from original code: cross-reference-console requirements remain upstream-reported; Echo-Merlini code attribution is retained; Artifact Two core remains atpprotocol; PR opener TMerlini/babyblueviper1 code is not converted into Pavlo sole authorship. P02/P03 incomplete historical source chains remain unresolved and are not release runtime dependencies. No source-author identity, sole ownership, independent operator or revenue percentage is inferred. Historical ledger claims are reported mechanical source evidence, not a fresh independent reconstruction of all 108 histories.\n\nThe catalog says22 bounded implementations; **21 named slices are supported after removing CHRONICLE-ROOTS\' nonexistent separate aggregate-root implementation** (PA-01). These counts include methods/interfaces and are not native full-profile counts. All74 entries have an audited transfer category in`audit-records.json`, using only RUNTIME_DEPENDENCY / PINNED_SOURCE_ADAPTER / REIMPLEMENTED_FROM_SPEC / METHODOLOGY_ONLY / FIXTURE_ONLY / HISTORICAL_LESSON / FUTURE_EXTENSION / NO_TRANSFERRED_CAPABILITY. FIXTURE_ONLY references can remain unimplemented/unselected; their used flag is explicit. Stochastic code is an original product extension; R4 contributes historical interface context only.\n\n| Repository | Audited transfer role(s) | Actual bounded capability records |\n|---|---|---|\n'
for r in repoRecords:md+=f"| {r['repository']} | {', '.join(r['auditContributionCategories'])} | {', '.join(r['auditImplementedCapabilityIds']) or 'None; reference/history/fixture account only'} |\n"
md+='\nPublic live selected-PR reads reconfirm PRF13 MERGED and PRF14 / recompute-kit65 / recompute-kit57 / MLDSA27 OPEN at their declared exact heads at 2026-10-11T18:42:11Z. Open experimental code is not relabeled main. Exact observation records appear in`provenance-check.json`.\n\nEvidence files:`provenance-check.json`, `source-path-check.json`, `nested-origin-pins.json`, `license-check.json`, `copied-license-scope.json`, `audit-records.json`. The QEV upstream LICENSING.md exact-ref scope confirms authored code/profile/test/tool/document grants and retains separate nested licenses/captured-provider exclusions; captured provider payloads were not selected. Only metadata references to historical captures exist in the selected native profile. The native NOTICE text\'s LICENSING.md reference is preserved verbatim; its source scope is independently read in`copied-license-scope.json`.\n\nThis audit did not rehash 21119 historical external snapshot files or inspect existing live worktrees. The frozen historical preservation report supports its dated build observation only. New public-source identity checks do not establish execution truth, source soundness, author independence, deployed origin or publication authority.\n'
